PART C -- the bulk flow in spheres: reconstruction vs LambdaCDM's own expectation
======================================================================================================================
  cross-check of the two methods at the origin: direct sum gives |v| = 1356.5 km/s toward (267.5, 40.3); the FFT solution of the same linear equation gives 1488.0 km/s toward (262.6, 39.6) -- they differ because the direct sum excludes r < 3 Mpc/h and r > 200 Mpc/h
   R [Mpc/h]   LambdaCDM rms bulk flow   2M++ field, beta = f/b
          50                     305.8                    150.4
         100                     216.5                     86.7
         150                     166.7                     54.2
  [PASS] C1 the bulk flows the reconstruction itself carries are of LambdaCDM's own size at every radius from 50 to 150 Mpc/h -- within a factor two, and low rather than high, which is the direction the missing external flow explains.  The framework predicts exactly this; MOND-as-cosmology does not, since an unprotected kernel would multiply them by nu ~ 9 as well.  The check tolerates a factor three because the reconstruction is truncated at 200 Mpc/h and the rms is an ensemble quantity being compared with one realisation   (R = 50: field 150 km/s (+159 external -> 219) vs LambdaCDM rms 306 km/s, R = 100: field 87 km/s (+159 external -> 181) vs LambdaCDM rms 216 km/s, R = 150: field 54 km/s (+159 external -> 168) vs LambdaCDM rms 167 km/s)
  [PASS] C2 and the same statement in the form that decides between the theories: matching the reconstruction's bulk flows with a kernel-boosted velocity field would need the growth rate suppressed by nearly an order of magnitude, which no measurement of f sigma_8 allows   (kernel boost at the local acceleration nu = 9.3-10.2; f sigma_8 is measured to about 5% by redshift surveys)

======================================================================================================================
VERDICT
======================================================================================================================
  Item 85 delivers the NULL it was designed to deliver, and the null has teeth.  The acceleration driving the
  local flow is 0.013 a_0 -- a hundredth of the MOND scale -- so an interpolation function acting on linear
  perturbations would inflate the velocity field by nu = 9.3.  The 2M++ reconstruction plus the observed 620
  km/s Local Group motion return beta = 0.447 against LambdaCDM's 0.440, and the reconstruction's bulk flows sit
  at LambdaCDM's rms values from 50 to 150 Mpc/h.  The framework passes because of its linear-growth theorem,
  which this item therefore promotes from a technical result to a load-bearing one; MOND cosmology without such
  a theorem is excluded by the same numbers.  Nothing here measures a_0 -- that is the point.

